{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter4#ex:tangential-connection-submanifold","title":"ex:tangential-connection-submanifold","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter4.md","line":89,"body":"","kind":"proof","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter4.tex#ex:tangential-connection-submanifold","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:normal-bundle]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter4#ex:euclidean-connection]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#prop:extension-smooth-function]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter4#prop:embedded-submanifold-covariant-derivative]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#exer:extension-smooth-function]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter4#prob:embedded-submanifold-covariant-derivative]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter4.tex","label":"ex:tangential-connection-submanifold","line":174,"source":"\\begin{example}[The Tangential Connection on a Submanifold of $\\mathbb{R}^n$]\n\\label{ex:tangential-connection-submanifold}\n\\uses{prop:normal-bundle, ex:euclidean-connection, prop:extension-smooth-function, prop:embedded-submanifold-covariant-derivative, prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames, exer:extension-smooth-function, prob:embedded-submanifold-covariant-derivative}\n\\dcref{ch4:4.9}\n\nFor an embedded $M\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$, define\n\\[\n\\nabla_X^TY=\\pi^T\\bigl(\\widetilde\\nabla_{\\widetilde X}\\widetilde Y|_M\\bigr),\n\\]\nwhere extensions are taken near $M$, $\\widetilde\\nabla$ is the Euclidean connection, and $\\pi^T$ is the tangential projection. This is independent of extensions by (4.4) and is a connection.\n\\end{example}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch Linearity in $X,Y$ is immediate. For an extension $\\widetilde f$ of $f$,\n\\[\n\\nabla_X^T(fY)=\\pi^T\\bigl(\\widetilde\\nabla_{\\widetilde X}(\\widetilde f\\widetilde Y)|_M\\bigr)=(Xf)Y+f\\nabla_X^TY.\n\\]\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p>\\begin{example} \\end{example}[The Tangential Connection on a Submanifold of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathbb {R}^n$\">$\\mathbb {R}^n$</span>] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-65783a74616e67656e7469616c2d636f6e6e656374696f6e2d7375626d616e69666f6c64\"></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Anormal-bundle\">↗ prop:normal-bundle</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter4%23ex%3Aeuclidean-connection\">↗ ex:euclidean-connection</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23prop%3Aextension-smooth-function\">↗ prop:extension-smooth-function</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter4%23prop%3Aembedded-submanifold-covariant-derivative\">↗ prop:embedded-submanifold-covariant-derivative</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Aadapted-orthonormal-frames\">↗ prop:adapted-orthonormal-frames</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23exer%3Aextension-smooth-function\">↗ exer:extension-smooth-function</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter4%23prob%3Aembedded-submanifold-covariant-derivative\">↗ prob:embedded-submanifold-covariant-derivative</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch4:4.9</span></span><p></p>For an embedded <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M\\subseteq \\mathbb R^n$\">$M\\subseteq \\mathbb R^n$</span>, define <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\nabla _X^TY=\\pi ^T\\bigl(\\widetilde\\nabla _{\\widetilde X}\\widetilde Y|_M\\bigr),  \\]\">\\[  \\nabla _X^TY=\\pi ^T\\bigl(\\widetilde\\nabla _{\\widetilde X}\\widetilde Y|_M\\bigr),  \\]</span> where extensions are taken near <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\widetilde\\nabla $\">$\\widetilde\\nabla $</span> is the Euclidean connection, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\pi ^T$\">$\\pi ^T$</span> is the tangential projection. This is independent of extensions by (4.4) and is a connection. \\end{example} <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Linearity in <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X,Y$\">$X,Y$</span> is immediate. For an extension <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\widetilde f$\">$\\widetilde f$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span>, </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\nabla _X^T(fY)=\\pi ^T\\bigl(\\widetilde\\nabla _{\\widetilde X}(\\widetilde f\\widetilde Y)|_M\\bigr)=(Xf)Y+f\\nabla _X^TY.  \\]\">\\[  \\nabla _X^T(fY)=\\pi ^T\\bigl(\\widetilde\\nabla _{\\widetilde X}(\\widetilde f\\widetilde Y)|_M\\bigr)=(Xf)Y+f\\nabla _X^TY.  \\]</span></p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: example、sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter4#ex:euclidean-connection","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter4#lem:connections-f